@title EPISODE 28 • TAPING TABLE
@bg indoor_training_facility
Mile repeats. Fifth rep. London's left ankle rolls on the bank and she goes down hard.
@show mayaellis
Maya Ellis: Don't move. Don't be a hero. Look at me. Scale of one to ten?
London: Three.
Maya Ellis: You're crying, London.
London: It's a dramatic three.
@show diggy
Diggy is across the facility before anyone else moves. He picks her up like she weighs nothing.
> [Bitchy] "Put me DOWN, I can walk." -> t1
> [Sweet] Hold onto his neck. Say nothing. -> t2
> [Bold] "If you drop me, Williams, I'm suing." -> t3
*t1
@add Diggy_Affection 1
Diggy: You can't. So you're gonna be mad AND carried.
@jump t_done
*t2
@add Diggy_Affection 3
@add Diggy_Trust 2
Her face is in his neck. He smells like cedar. Coach Holloway, watching, looks away like she's giving them privacy.
@jump t_done
*t3
@add Diggy_Affection 2
Diggy: (laughing) With your dad's lawyers? I'll be careful.
*t_done
@bg trainer_room
@show mayaellis
Maya Ellis: Sprain. Two weeks, maybe three. If you're smart.
London: I'm never smart.
Maya Ellis: I know. Half the secrets on this team get told on this table, you know. You can tell me one too. It's free.
> [Sweet] "I think I'm in love with him and I'm scared." -> m1
> [Bitchy] "I don't have secrets. I have strategy." -> m2
> [Good] "I'm scared I'll never be as fast again." -> m3
*m1
@add London_Confidence 2
@add Love_Admitted 1
Maya Ellis: (wrapping the ankle) Being scared and being in love look exactly the same from the inside. Ask anyone married.
@jump m_done
*m2
@add London_Confidence -1
Maya Ellis: Mm-hm. That boy's been outside the door for forty minutes. Strategy that.
@jump m_done
*m3
@add Coach_Respect 2
Maya Ellis: You will. I've seen a hundred ankles. Yours is boring. That's a compliment.
*m_done
Maya Ellis: (finishing the tape) One more thing. Being hurt doesn't pause your recovery plan. Same check-ins with me, same appointments. Being out of training can mess with your head. You call me if it does. Deal?
London: (quietly) Deal.
She means it. Two years ago she wouldn't have.
@show holloway
Holloway: (in the doorway) Sterling. You're out for conference indoors.
London: Coach—
Holloway: Out. But you're traveling with us. Somebody has to yell at Priya. You're good at it now.
That's the nicest thing Holloway has ever said to her.
@load s1/ep29.mvs
